      "title": null,
      "gender": "Female",
      "race": "Merfolk",
      "subrace": null,
      "description": "The little mermaid's wise grandmother, who tells her of the world above the waves and of the soul only humans possess.",
      "personality": "Wise and fond of her granddaughters, happy to indulge their curiosity about the human world.",
      "motivation": "Wants to prepare the little mermaid for the world above, even while doubting she will ever truly reach it.",
      "qualities": "Knowledgeable about both mermaid tradition and human customs, a rare bridge between the two.",
      "weaknesses": "Her warnings about the price of a soul go unheeded once the little mermaid's mind is made up.",
      "biography": "The Sea King's mother, who first tells the little mermaid about the immortal soul that only humans possess.",
      "plannedTimeline": "Remains in the Sea Kingdom, her warnings about the cost of an immortal soul proven true by the story's end.",
